  "details": "Communities that host large-scale events often have to make several moderators \"spawncamp\" the world spawn, and patrol the instance, looking for people in \"Very Poor\" or generally unoptimized avatars.\n\nThere exists no way to create an allowed API application to show performance rank of private avatars, due to the file ID being hidden. (E.G. VRCX)\n\nIf you expose the performance rank via a log line, this would improve the QoL for many of VRChats biggest event spaces.\n\nThere already exists a log on avatar change, example being:\n\n\"[Behaviour] Switching HarperSmile to avatar Harper the Durgarra V2․1\"\n\nIf you simply append the returned avatar performance rank, or add a new log line that attributes an Avatar Name to Avatar Rank, it would assist greatly!",
